# Orchestra poll-and-wake for one lane (tools/wake/linux/crontab.example).
#
# Install this with `crontab -e`, replacing the two REPLACE values if this lane
# does not keep its waker in ~/.orchestra/wake. Keep the line on ONE line: cron
# needs the five time fields and then the command.
#
# The script holds a lock, so ticks that fire while a wait is still running exit
# instead of polling twice; --timeout 240 keeps one cron run shorter than the
# five-minute tick. The wake command itself is in wake.env, so cron never parses
# it. cron runs this under /bin/sh with HOME set, so $HOME expands.
#
# m    h  dom mon dow   command
*/5 * * * *  $HOME/.orchestra/wake/wake.sh --env-file $HOME/.orchestra/wake/wake.env --timeout 240 >>$HOME/.orchestra/wake/cron.out 2>&1
